  "title": "Tourte de blettes niçoise",
  "subtitle": "Niçoise sweet Swiss chard tart with raisins, pine nuts and apple",
  "excerpt": "Tourte de blettes is the traditional Christmas dessert of Nice: a closed double-crust tart filled with a mixture of Swiss chard leaves, raisins, pine nuts, apple, and sugar. The chard is not a flavouring but the principal ingredient; its mild, slightly vegetal note becomes entirely sweet and fragrant in the filling. It is one of the thirteen traditional Provençal Christmas desserts and a good deal more accessible than it sounds.",
