  "sourceType": "CLASSIC",
  "sourceNotes": "Tourte de blettes is listed among the thirteen traditional Provençal desserts served at the Gros Souper (Christmas Eve feast). It is a Niçoise speciality documented in books on Niçois and Provençal food including Jacques Médecin's La Cuisine du Comté de Nice (1972, English translation Cuisine Niçoise, 1983). Médecin includes both a sweet version (with raisins and pine nuts) and a savoury version; the sweet version is the Christmas tradition. The recipe is documented in cookery references and Niçois food-heritage sources.",
