  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tourte de blettes is a conversation starter: Swiss chard, raisins, and pine nuts in a sweet tart sounds improbable and tastes entirely natural. The chard must be squeezed very dry after wilting or the filling will be watery. Everything else is just assembly: spread the filling, top with a pastry lid, press the edges to seal, and bake until deep golden. Dust generously with icing sugar while still warm."
          }
        ]
      },
