      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make the pastry"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Rub {{unsalted-butter}} into {{plain-flour}}, {{caster-sugar}} (30 g), and {{sea-salt-fine}} until the mixture resembles breadcrumbs. Add 1 beaten {{eggs}} and {{olive-oil}} and press together to form a dough, adding a teaspoon of cold water if needed. Divide in two equal halves. Wrap and refrigerate for 30 minutes."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Prepare the chard filling"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Wash {{chard}} leaves and wilt in a large dry pan over a medium heat for 2 to 3 minutes until collapsed. Tip into a colander and leave to cool, then squeeze very firmly in a clean cloth until as dry as possible. Chop coarsely. Combine the chopped chard, diced {{apple-eating}}, {{raisins}}, {{pine-nuts}}, {{caster-sugar}} (100 g), the zest of {{lemon}}, and the remaining 2 beaten {{eggs}} in a large bowl and mix well."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Assemble and bake"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Heat the oven to 190°C (conventional). Grease a 24 cm tart tin. Roll one disc of pastry and line the tin. Fill with the chard mixture, spreading it level. Roll the second disc and lay it over the filling. Press the edges together firmly to seal and trim any overhang. Pierce the lid 6 times with a fork. Bake for 40 to 45 minutes until the crust is deep golden. Dust with {{icing-sugar}} while still warm and serve at room temperature."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
